import AFTD.Prelude

/-!
# IsCentralDihedralExtension

Topic: graphs   Node: bff87e2eaf1d

Provenance: formalization of a published result. Source: arXiv:2610.33692, Theorem 2(b2)

A finite group $G$ is a central extension $\widehat{D}_{4m}$ of the dihedral group $D_{2m}$ if $|G| = 4m$ and $G$ is generated by elements $a$ of order $m$ and $b$ of order 4 satisfying $b^{-1} a b = a^{-1}$.
-/

/-- A group of order 4m generated by elements a of order m and b of order 4 satisfying b⁻¹ab = a⁻¹ is a central extension of the dihedral group D_{2m}. -/
def IsCentralDihedralExtension (G : Type*) [Group G] (m : ℕ) : Prop := Nat.card G = 4 * m ∧
  ∃ (a b : G), orderOf a = m ∧ orderOf b = 4 ∧ b⁻¹ * a * b = a⁻¹ ∧
    Subgroup.closure ({a, b} : Set G) = ⊤
